1result.sql
```

Reason:  
The query in 1result.sql:

• looks within the same session for an occurrence of “/regist/input” that is earlier than an occurrence of “/regist/confirm” (self‑join on stamp ordering).  
• counts each qualifying session only once via COUNT(DISTINCT session).  

This logic correctly captures every session that ever had the required page order, even when the session also contains extra views (e.g. confirm → input → confirm).  
The alternative aggregation solution (2result.sql) could miss such cases because it compares only the earliest confirm to the earliest input, while the quoted‑identifier version (0result.sql) relies on vendor‑specific quoting. Hence 1result.sql is the safest and clearest correct answer.